X-WR-TIMEZONE:Europe/Amsterdam
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-08-27-run-1700@marathon2027
DTSTAMP:20260827T070309Z
DTSTART:20260827T170000
DTEND:20260827T174500
SUMMARY:🏃 Easy run 5 km
DESCRIPTION:Week B1\n\n5 km at easy pace\, 5:35–6:00/km\, heart rate un
 der 145. Conversational the whole way — the cyclist's engine will want
  to go faster\; the legs don't get a vote yet\, so don't let it. First r
 un of the block. Two runs this week is the whole week — it's already W
 ednesday.
CATEGORIES:run
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-08-29-run-0900@marathon2027
DTSTAMP:20260827T070309Z
DTSTART:20260829T090000
DTEND:20260829T095800
SUMMARY:🏃 Easy run 8 km
DESCRIPTION:Week B1\n\n8 km at easy pace\, 5:35–6:00/km\, heart rate un
 der 145. Conversational the whole way — the cyclist's engine will want
  to go faster\; the legs don't get a vote yet\, so don't let it. 
CATEGORIES:run
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-08-25-bike-0645@marathon2027
DTSTAMP:20260827T070309Z
DTSTART:20260825T064500
DTEND:20260825T074500
SUMMARY:🚴 Bike — hard session
DESCRIPTION:Week B1\n\nYour own session — Z4/Z5\, as now.\n\n45–60 mi
 nutes. This is one of the week's three hard days (bike Tue\, run Wed\, l
 ong run Sat).
CATEGORIES:bike
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-08-27-bike-0645@marathon2027
DTSTAMP:20260827T070309Z
DTSTART:20260827T064500
DTEND:20260827T073500
SUMMARY:🚴 Bike — hard session (base: your own)
DESCRIPTION:Week B1\n\nYour own session — Z4/Z5\, as now.\n\nBase phase
 : this can stay hard — run quality is only strides until October\, so 
 nothing clashes. From 19 Oct it becomes Z2.
CATEGORIES:bike
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-08-26-bike-1800@marathon2027
DTSTAMP:20260827T070309Z
DTSTART:20260826T180000
DTEND:20260826T190000
SUMMARY:🚴 Bike — 60' Z2 (optional)
DESCRIPTION:Week B1\n\nOptional. 60 minutes Z2 at most — under 145 bpm.
  The old 70 km Wednesday evening ride is gone for the duration\; if you 
 ride\, it's a spin. Not at all in the block.
CATEGORIES:bike
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-08-30-bike-0930@marathon2027
DTSTAMP:20260827T070309Z
DTSTART:20260830T093000
DTEND:20260830T133000
SUMMARY:🚴 Long ride — Z2\, max 4 h
DESCRIPTION:Week B1\n\nThe one long ride of the week. Z2: heart rate unde
 r 145\, under 240 W. Cap 4 h — that's a ceiling\, not a target. Yester
 day was the long run\, so this is a flush\; if the group ride turns into
  a hammerfest\, drop off. No back-to-back 100 km days in the block.
CATEGORIES:bike
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-08-24-gym-1230@marathon2027
DTSTAMP:20260827T070309Z
DTSTART:20260824T123000
DTEND:20260824T133000
SUMMARY:🏋️ Chest & triceps + Core A
DESCRIPTION:Week B1\n\nBench or DB press 3×6–8\nIncline DB press 3×8
 –10\nDips or push-ups 3×8–10\nTriceps pushdown / overhead extension
  3×10\n\nCore A (15'): dead bug 3×8/side · Pallof press 3×10/side ·
  front plank 3×45 s · hanging knee raise 3×10.\n\nKeep it to 45–60 
 min so Monday stays a recovery day for the legs.
CATEGORIES:gym
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-08-26-gym-1230@marathon2027
DTSTAMP:20260827T070309Z
DTSTART:20260826T123000
DTEND:20260826T133000
SUMMARY:🏋️ Back & biceps + Core B
DESCRIPTION:Week B1\n\nRows 3×6–8\nPull-ups or lat pulldown 3×6–10\
 nFace pulls 3×12 — posture late in the marathon\nCurls 3×10\n\nCore 
 B (15'): side plank 3×30 s/side · bird dog 3×8/side · suitcase carry
  3×30 m/side.\n\nLunchtime or morning — not right before the evening 
 quality run.
CATEGORIES:gym
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-08-27-gym-1800@marathon2027
DTSTAMP:20260827T070309Z
DTSTART:20260827T180000
DTEND:20260827T190000
SUMMARY:🏋️ Heavy legs
DESCRIPTION:Week B1\n\nBack squat 60×15 warm-up\, 120×5\, 120×5\, 130
 ×5\, 130×5–6\nSingle-leg RDL 4×7/leg at 60–65 kg\nBulgarian split
  squat 3×7/leg at 40 kg\nSingle-leg calf raise (straight knee) 3×10/le
 g\, 3 s down\nBent-knee / seated calf raise 3×12 — soleus\nSeated leg
  curl 3×8/leg at 35 kg\n\nNo running today — bike this morning\, legs
  this evening. Nothing to failure\; you're running long in 48 h.
CATEGORIES:gym
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-08-28-mobility-1230@marathon2027
DTSTAMP:20260827T070309Z
DTSTART:20260828T123000
DTEND:20260828T131000
SUMMARY:🧘 Mobility + leg maintenance
DESCRIPTION:Week B1\n\nNo running today. Injury-prevention session — no
 thing to failure\, nothing that leaves you sore on Saturday.\n\n1. Mobil
 ity (10'): couch stretch 2×60 s/side · 90/90 hip switches 2×8 · ankl
 e dorsiflexion wall touches 2×10/side · thoracic rotations 2×8/side\n
 2. Strength-light (12'): banded lateral walks 3×12/side · single-leg g
 lute bridge 3×10/side · Copenhagen plank 3×20 s/side\n3. Nordic curls
  2×4 — the best eccentric hamstring work there is. Sore for the first
  few weeks\; that's why they start now\, not in December.\n4. Step-downs
  off a box 2×10/side\, slow · single-leg balance\n5. Dead bug or Pallo
 f if time
CATEGORIES:mobility
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-08-31-run-0730@marathon2027
DTSTAMP:20260827T070309Z
DTSTART:20260831T073000
DTEND:20260831T081500
SUMMARY:🏃 Easy run 6 km
DESCRIPTION:Week B2\n\n6 km at easy pace\, 5:35–6:00/km\, heart rate un
 der 145. Conversational the whole way — the cyclist's engine will want
  to go faster\; the legs don't get a vote yet\, so don't let it. 
CATEGORIES:run
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-09-02-run-1800@marathon2027
DTSTAMP:20260827T070309Z
DTSTART:20260902T180000
DTEND:20260902T190000
SUMMARY:🏃 Easy run 5 km + strides
DESCRIPTION:Week B2\n\n5 km at easy pace\, 5:35–6:00/km\, heart rate un
 der 145. Conversational the whole way — the cyclist's engine will want
  to go faster\; the legs don't get a vote yet\, so don't let it. Finish 
 with 6 × 20–25 s strides\, building to about mile pace\, relaxed\, fu
 ll walk-back between. They keep leg speed while everything else is slow.
  
CATEGORIES:run
END:VEVENT
