DTSTART:20260917T180000
DTEND:20260917T190000
SUMMARY:🏋️ Heavy legs
DESCRIPTION:Week B4\n\nBack squat 60×15 warm-up\, 120×5\, 120×5\, 130
 ×5\, 130×5–6\nSingle-leg RDL 4×7/leg at 60–65 kg\nBulgarian split
  squat 3×7/leg at 40 kg\nSingle-leg calf raise (straight knee) 3×10/le
 g\, 3 s down\nBent-knee / seated calf raise 3×12 — soleus\nSeated leg
  curl 3×8/leg at 35 kg\n\nNo running today — bike this morning\, legs
  this evening. Nothing to failure\; you're running long in 48 h.
CATEGORIES:gym
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-09-18-mobility-1230@marathon2027
DTSTAMP:20260827T070309Z
DTSTART:20260918T123000
DTEND:20260918T131000
SUMMARY:🧘 Mobility + leg maintenance
DESCRIPTION:Week B4\n\nNo running today. Injury-prevention session — no
 thing to failure\, nothing that leaves you sore on Saturday.\n\n1. Mobil
 ity (10'): couch stretch 2×60 s/side · 90/90 hip switches 2×8 · ankl
 e dorsiflexion wall touches 2×10/side · thoracic rotations 2×8/side\n
 2. Strength-light (12'): banded lateral walks 3×12/side · single-leg g
 lute bridge 3×10/side · Copenhagen plank 3×20 s/side\n3. Nordic curls
  2×4 — the best eccentric hamstring work there is. Sore for the first
  few weeks\; that's why they start now\, not in December.\n4. Step-downs
  off a box 2×10/side\, slow · single-leg balance\n5. Dead bug or Pallo
 f if time
CATEGORIES:mobility
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-09-21-run-0730@marathon2027
DTSTAMP:20260827T070309Z
DTSTART:20260921T073000
DTEND:20260921T081500
SUMMARY:🏃 Easy run 6 km
DESCRIPTION:Week B5\n\n6 km at easy pace\, 5:35–6:00/km\, heart rate un
 der 145. Conversational the whole way — the cyclist's engine will want
  to go faster\; the legs don't get a vote yet\, so don't let it. 
CATEGORIES:run
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-09-23-run-1800@marathon2027
DTSTAMP:20260827T070309Z
DTSTART:20260923T180000
DTEND:20260923T190000
SUMMARY:🏃 Easy run 6 km + strides
DESCRIPTION:Week B5\n\n6 km at easy pace\, 5:35–6:00/km\, heart rate un
 der 145. Conversational the whole way — the cyclist's engine will want
  to go faster\; the legs don't get a vote yet\, so don't let it. Finish 
 with 6 × 20–25 s strides\, building to about mile pace\, relaxed\, fu
 ll walk-back between. They keep leg speed while everything else is slow.
  
CATEGORIES:run
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-09-26-run-0900@marathon2027
DTSTAMP:20260827T070309Z
DTSTART:20260926T090000
DTEND:20260926T101000
SUMMARY:🏃 Easy run 10 km
DESCRIPTION:Week B5\n\n10 km at easy pace\, 5:35–6:00/km\, heart rate u
 nder 145. Conversational the whole way — the cyclist's engine will wan
 t to go faster\; the legs don't get a vote yet\, so don't let it. 
CATEGORIES:run
END:VEVENT
