SUMMARY:🏋️ Heavy legs
DESCRIPTION:Week W3\n\nBack squat 3×5 at 125–130 (after warm-up)\nSing
 le-leg RDL 3×7/leg\nBulgarian split squat 3×7/leg\nSingle-leg calf rai
 se 3×10/leg\, 3 s down\nSeated calf raise 3×12\nSeated leg curl 3×8/l
 eg\n\nSame weights as base\, one fewer set. No PR attempts from here.
CATEGORIES:gym
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-11-06-mobility-1230@marathon2027
DTSTAMP:20260827T070309Z
DTSTART:20261106T123000
DTEND:20261106T131000
SUMMARY:🧘 Mobility + leg maintenance
DESCRIPTION:Week W3\n\nNo running today. Injury-prevention session — no
 thing to failure\, nothing that leaves you sore on Saturday.\n\n1. Mobil
 ity (10'): couch stretch 2×60 s/side · 90/90 hip switches 2×8 · ankl
 e dorsiflexion wall touches 2×10/side · thoracic rotations 2×8/side\n
 2. Strength-light (12'): banded lateral walks 3×12/side · single-leg g
 lute bridge 3×10/side · Copenhagen plank 3×20 s/side\n3. Nordic curls
  2×4 — the best eccentric hamstring work there is. Sore for the first
  few weeks\; that's why they start now\, not in December.\n4. Step-downs
  off a box 2×10/side\, slow · single-leg balance\n5. Dead bug or Pallo
 f if time
CATEGORIES:mobility
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-11-06-swim-0700@marathon2027
DTSTAMP:20260827T070309Z
DTSTART:20261106T070000
DTEND:20261106T074000
SUMMARY:🏊 Swim 30–40'
DESCRIPTION:Week W3\n\nSteady swim building toward a continuous 2 km by e
 arly December. 1.9 km = 76 lengths of a 25 m pool. Bilateral breathing\,
  no drills needed — you can already swim\; this is about the feel and 
 the shoulders on 13 Dec.
CATEGORIES:swim
