BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2027-01-11-gym-1230@marathon2027
DTSTAMP:20260827T070309Z
DTSTART:20270111T123000
DTEND:20270111T133000
SUMMARY:🏋️ Chest & triceps + Core A
DESCRIPTION:Week W13\n\nBench or DB press 3×6–8\nIncline DB press 3×8
 –10\nDips or push-ups 3×8–10\nTriceps pushdown / overhead extension
  3×10\n\nCore A (15'): dead bug 3×8/side · Pallof press 3×10/side ·
  front plank 3×45 s · hanging knee raise 3×10.\n\nKeep it to 45–60 
 min so Monday stays a recovery day for the legs.
CATEGORIES:gym
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2027-01-13-gym-1230@marathon2027
DTSTAMP:20260827T070309Z
DTSTART:20270113T123000
DTEND:20270113T133000
SUMMARY:🏋️ Back & biceps + Core B
DESCRIPTION:Week W13\n\nRows 3×6–8\nPull-ups or lat pulldown 3×6–10
 \nFace pulls 3×12 — posture late in the marathon\nCurls 3×10\n\nCore
  B (15'): side plank 3×30 s/side · bird dog 3×8/side · suitcase carr
 y 3×30 m/side.\n\nLunchtime or morning — not right before the evening
  quality run.
CATEGORIES:gym
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2027-01-14-gym-1800@marathon2027
DTSTAMP:20260827T070309Z
DTSTART:20270114T180000
DTEND:20270114T183500
SUMMARY:🏋️ Legs — maintenance
DESCRIPTION:Week W13\n\nBack squat 3×5\, same weight\, no PRs\nSingle-le
 g RDL 2×7/leg\nSingle-leg calf raise 3×10/leg\, 3 s down\nSeated calf 
 raise 3×12\nSeated leg curl 2×8/leg\nSplit squats: 2×7 light\, or dro
 p\n\nMaintenance: 2 working sets\, nothing new. The point is to keep str
 ength and tendon stiffness without costing Saturday.
CATEGORIES:gym
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2027-01-15-mobility-1230@marathon2027
DTSTAMP:20260827T070309Z
DTSTART:20270115T123000
DTEND:20270115T131000
SUMMARY:🧘 Mobility + leg maintenance
DESCRIPTION:Week W13\n\nNo running today. Injury-prevention session — n
 othing to failure\, nothing that leaves you sore on Saturday.\n\n1. Mobi
 lity (10'): couch stretch 2×60 s/side · 90/90 hip switches 2×8 · ank
 le dorsiflexion wall touches 2×10/side · thoracic rotations 2×8/side\
 n2. Strength-light (12'): banded lateral walks 3×12/side · single-leg 
 glute bridge 3×10/side · Copenhagen plank 3×20 s/side\n3. Nordic curl
 s 2×4 — the best eccentric hamstring work there is. Sore for the firs
 t few weeks\; that's why they start now\, not in December.\n4. Step-down
 s off a box 2×10/side\, slow · single-leg balance\n5. Dead bug or Pall
 of if time
CATEGORIES:mobility
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2027-01-18-run-0730@marathon2027
DTSTAMP:20260827T070309Z
DTSTART:20270118T073000
DTEND:20270118T081500
SUMMARY:🏃 Easy run 8 km + strides
DESCRIPTION:Week W14\n\n8 km at easy pace\, 5:35–6:00/km\, heart rate u
 nder 145. Conversational the whole way — the cyclist's engine will wan
 t to go faster\; the legs don't get a vote yet\, so don't let it. Finish
  with 6 × 20–25 s strides\, building to about mile pace\, relaxed\, f
 ull walk-back between. They keep leg speed while everything else is slow
 . 
CATEGORIES:run
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2027-01-19-run-1730@marathon2027
DTSTAMP:20260827T070309Z
DTSTART:20270119T173000
DTEND:20270119T181000
SUMMARY:🏃 Optional easy 6 km + strides
DESCRIPTION:Week W14\n\nOptional. 6 km at easy pace\, 5:35–6:00/km\, he
 art rate under 145. Conversational the whole way — the cyclist's engin
 e will want to go faster\; the legs don't get a vote yet\, so don't let 
 it. Finish with 6 × 20–25 s strides\, building to about mile pace\, r
 elaxed\, full walk-back between. They keep leg speed while everything el
 se is slow.  If Tuesday's bike session was big\, skip this.
CATEGORIES:run
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2027-01-20-run-1800@marathon2027
DTSTAMP:20260827T070309Z
DTSTART:20270120T180000
DTEND:20270120T191500
SUMMARY:🏃 Threshold 5 × 1 mile
DESCRIPTION:Week W14\n\nWarm up 3 km easy + 4 strides. 5 × 1 mile (1.6 k
 m) at threshold with 90 s jog. Cool down 2 km easy. Paces: easy 5:35–6
 :00 (HR <145) · MP 5:12–5:20 · T 4:40–4:48 · 10k 4:22–4:28 · I
  4:05–4:12 (800 ≈ 3:20\, 1k ≈ 4:08). Re-set after the 5k TT (17 Oc
 t) and the January half.
CATEGORIES:run
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2027-01-23-run-0900@marathon2027
DTSTAMP:20260827T070309Z
DTSTART:20270123T090000
DTEND:20270123T122200
SUMMARY:🏃 Long run 32 km
DESCRIPTION:Week W14\n\nAll at easy pace\, 5:35–6:00/km\, HR under 145.
  Walk breaks are fine. Gel at 40' and every 30–35' after. The peak lon
 g run. Easy to 24 km\, then the last 8 km at marathon pace. If you're go
 ing self-supported\, run this on your race loop with the bag stash and (
 if you have one) the friend on the bike — this is the rehearsal. Paces
 : easy 5:35–6:00 (HR <145) · MP 5:12–5:20 · T 4:40–4:48 · 10k 4
 :22–4:28 · I 4:05–4:12 (800 ≈ 3:20\, 1k ≈ 4:08). Re-set after t
 he 5k TT (17 Oct) and the January half.
CATEGORIES:run
END:VEVENT
