UID:2027-02-04-gym-1800@marathon2027
DTSTAMP:20260827T070309Z
DTSTART:20270204T180000
DTEND:20270204T183000
SUMMARY:🏋️ Legs — last heavy session (light)
DESCRIPTION:Week W16\n\nLast leg session before the race. 2 sets of every
 thing at 70%: squat 2×5 at ~110\, RDL 2×7/leg\, both calf raises 2×10
 \, leg curl 2×8. Done by 4 Feb\; from here legs only get the Friday mob
 ility.
CATEGORIES:gym
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2027-02-05-mobility-1230@marathon2027
DTSTAMP:20260827T070309Z
DTSTART:20270205T123000
DTEND:20270205T131000
SUMMARY:🧘 Mobility + leg maintenance
DESCRIPTION:Week W16\n\nNo running today. Injury-prevention session — n
 othing to failure\, nothing that leaves you sore on Saturday.\n\n1. Mobi
 lity (10'): couch stretch 2×60 s/side · 90/90 hip switches 2×8 · ank
 le dorsiflexion wall touches 2×10/side · thoracic rotations 2×8/side\
 n2. Strength-light (12'): banded lateral walks 3×12/side · single-leg 
 glute bridge 3×10/side · Copenhagen plank 3×20 s/side\n3. Nordic curl
 s 2×4 — the best eccentric hamstring work there is. Sore for the firs
 t few weeks\; that's why they start now\, not in December.\n4. Step-down
 s off a box 2×10/side\, slow · single-leg balance\n5. Dead bug or Pall
 of if time
CATEGORIES:mobility
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2027-02-08-run-0730@marathon2027
DTSTAMP:20260827T070309Z
DTSTART:20270208T073000
DTEND:20270208T081500
SUMMARY:🏃 Easy run 6 km + strides
DESCRIPTION:Week W17\n\n6 km at easy pace\, 5:35–6:00/km\, heart rate u
 nder 145. Conversational the whole way — the cyclist's engine will wan
 t to go faster\; the legs don't get a vote yet\, so don't let it. Finish
  with 6 × 20–25 s strides\, building to about mile pace\, relaxed\, f
 ull walk-back between. They keep leg speed while everything else is slow
 . 
CATEGORIES:run
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2027-02-09-run-1730@marathon2027
DTSTAMP:20260827T070309Z
DTSTART:20270209T173000
DTEND:20270209T181000
SUMMARY:🏃 Optional easy 5 km + strides
DESCRIPTION:Week W17\n\nOptional. 5 km at easy pace\, 5:35–6:00/km\, he
 art rate under 145. Conversational the whole way — the cyclist's engin
 e will want to go faster\; the legs don't get a vote yet\, so don't let 
 it. Finish with 6 × 20–25 s strides\, building to about mile pace\, r
 elaxed\, full walk-back between. They keep leg speed while everything el
 se is slow.  If Tuesday's bike session was big\, skip this.
CATEGORIES:run
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2027-02-10-run-1800@marathon2027
DTSTAMP:20260827T070309Z
DTSTART:20270210T180000
DTEND:20270210T190000
SUMMARY:🏃 Sharpener 4 × 1 km
DESCRIPTION:Week W17\n\nWarm up 3 km easy + 4 strides. 4 × 1 km at 10k p
 ace with 400 m jog. Cool down 2 km easy. Paces: easy 5:35–6:00 (HR <14
 5) · MP 5:12–5:20 · T 4:40–4:48 · 10k 4:22–4:28 · I 4:05–4:1
 2 (800 ≈ 3:20\, 1k ≈ 4:08). Re-set after the 5k TT (17 Oct) and the 
 January half.
CATEGORIES:run
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2027-02-13-run-0900@marathon2027
DTSTAMP:20260827T070309Z
DTSTART:20270213T090000
DTEND:20270213T103400
SUMMARY:🏃 Long run 14 km
DESCRIPTION:Week W17\n\nAll at easy pace\, 5:35–6:00/km\, HR under 145.
  Walk breaks are fine. Gel at 40' and every 30–35' after. 5 km at mara
 thon pace in the middle. Short\, controlled\, done. Paces: easy 5:35–6
 :00 (HR <145) · MP 5:12–5:20 · T 4:40–4:48 · 10k 4:22–4:28 · I
  4:05–4:12 (800 ≈ 3:20\, 1k ≈ 4:08). Re-set after the 5k TT (17 Oc
 t) and the January half.
CATEGORIES:run
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
