DTSTAMP:20260827T070309Z
DTSTART:20270209T064500
DTEND:20270209T074500
SUMMARY:🚴 Bike — Z2
DESCRIPTION:Week W17\n\nZ2 only: heart rate under 145\, under 240 W. It w
 ill feel pointless. That's the point — this is what lets Wednesday and
  Saturday be good.
CATEGORIES:bike
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2027-02-11-bike-0645@marathon2027
DTSTAMP:20260827T070309Z
DTSTART:20270211T064500
DTEND:20270211T073500
SUMMARY:🚴 Bike — Z2
DESCRIPTION:Week W17\n\nZ2 only: heart rate under 145\, under 240 W. It w
 ill feel pointless. That's the point — this is what lets Wednesday and
  Saturday be good.\n\n45–60 minutes. Heavy legs this evening. No runni
 ng today.
CATEGORIES:bike
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2027-02-14-bike-0930@marathon2027
DTSTAMP:20260827T070309Z
DTSTART:20270214T093000
DTEND:20270214T103000
SUMMARY:🚴 Long ride — Z2\, max 1 h
DESCRIPTION:Week W17\n\nThe one long ride of the week. Z2: heart rate und
 er 145\, under 240 W. Cap 1 h — that's a ceiling\, not a target. Yeste
 rday was the long run\, so this is a flush\; if the group ride turns int
 o a hammerfest\, drop off. No back-to-back 100 km days in the block.
CATEGORIES:bike
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2027-02-08-gym-1230@marathon2027
DTSTAMP:20260827T070309Z
DTSTART:20270208T123000
DTEND:20270208T131000
SUMMARY:🏋️ Chest & triceps + Core A (light\, 2 sets)
DESCRIPTION:Week W17\n\nBench or DB press 3×6–8\nIncline DB press 3×8
 –10\nDips or push-ups 3×8–10\nTriceps pushdown / overhead extension
  3×10\n\nCore A (15'): dead bug 3×8/side · Pallof press 3×10/side ·
  front plank 3×45 s · hanging knee raise 3×10.\n\nKeep it to 45–60 
 min so Monday stays a recovery day for the legs.\n\nTaper: 2 sets of eve
 rything\, moderate weight\, nothing to failure. Keep the core work.
CATEGORIES:gym
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2027-02-10-gym-1230@marathon2027
DTSTAMP:20260827T070309Z
DTSTART:20270210T123000
DTEND:20270210T131000
SUMMARY:🏋️ Back & biceps + Core B (light\, 2 sets)
DESCRIPTION:Week W17\n\nRows 3×6–8\nPull-ups or lat pulldown 3×6–10
 \nFace pulls 3×12 — posture late in the marathon\nCurls 3×10\n\nCore
  B (15'): side plank 3×30 s/side · bird dog 3×8/side · suitcase carr
 y 3×30 m/side.\n\nLunchtime or morning — not right before the evening
  quality run.\n\nTaper: 2 sets of everything\, moderate weight\, nothing
  to failure. Keep the core work.
CATEGORIES:gym
END:VEVENT
